implementationPlan.description:
One adversarial self-review of the F05 diff only (load adversarial-self-review). Write one mutant per clause, and confirm each focused-suite survivor on the FULL suite before calling it unpinned (mem gotcha-mutation-or-chain-clauses). The mutants:
- the event gate's PLAN_APPROVED clause alone, and its PLAN_AUTO_APPROVED clause alone;
- the gate widened to any event;
- SPEED stamping the fire-time revision instead of the armed one;
- the catch widened beyond PLAN_REVISION_MISMATCH;
- the AWAITING_APPROVAL re-check removed;
- re-arm binding the current revision instead of the snapshot's;
- re-arm without the legacy fallback;
- re-arm without the per-row try/catch;
- TURBO without the stamp.

Also check:
- two timers for one task, and an identical resubmission (ABA);
- absent, malformed and unsafe revisions;
- a restart with and without a snapshot;
- the strict guard and NOT_READY precedence are untouched;
- relaxed set_task_status and omitted-token human approvals still stamp nothing (F04's tests).

Docs are handed to F12: the architect's comment on task-72184c65 lists MCP_SERVER.md, PLAN_APPROVAL_FRESHNESS.md and SCHEMA.md. Add a follow-up comment there only if the implementation deviates from it. No Git writes: the wrapper lands the work.
